FUN_1000_a401 / a395 / FUN_0000_7cd5 (per-object UPDATE cascade, reached via c0e5->7c1d, patches 243/244):
GS-relative table base-loss SIGSEGV in a401 + dropped return-CF in a401/a395 that 7cd5 consumes.

ROOT CAUSE (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin; gdb crash at fist.c a401 line +0x2b84 access).
7c1d's first callee 7cd5 (asm 0x7cd5) runs the object's steering/limit update: `lcall a401; jae..; lcall
a395; jb..; lcall a1d6; obj[4]+=obj[0x59]; obj[8]+=obj[0x5b]`.  The two lcalls return a condition in CF
(x86 stc/clc + lret) that 7cd5 branches on (a401 CF=1 -> obj[0xcb]=3; a395 CF=0 -> obj[0xca]=3 + 76e8).
Ghidra has no x86-16 flag convention -> folded CF to a constant 0 (in_CF) AND, in a401, base-lost the
GS-segment table lookup (asm 1a446 `mov 0x70,%gs`; gs = word[DGROUP:0x70] = the STRSEG resource segment)
to an ABSOLUTE HOST offset `+0x2b84` -> wild deref SIGSEGV on the first per-frame object update.

FIX (all three, asm-verified): (a401) reconstruct the GS-relative colour/limit-table read at gs<<4 base
(word[gs:0x2b84+idx] then byte[gs:clamp+off]) + set g_fist_cf per return point (1a49e stc=adjusted /
1a4a0 clc=early); (a395, pure object-relative, no crash) set g_fist_cf per return (1a3fd clc=moved /
1a3ff stc=early); (7cd5) branch on g_fist_cf instead of the folded in_CF.  Object accesses are all
DS:DI-relative (host-pointer correct via the object pointer 7c1d threads).  Mission-cascade only.
